 ## Background
-The Plenoxels method was introduced by Lipp et al. in 2022 [S1]. It utilizes sparse voxel grids and spherical harmonics to represent radiance fields without neural networks, enabling fast rendering and optimization [S1]. The regularization strategies described herein were developed to address the instability and memory issues associated with optimizing high-dimensional SH coefficients in sparse voxel structures [S1]. The implementation relies on custom CUDA extensions for differentiable volume rendering due to limited support in standard autodiff libraries [S1].
